media: nxp: dwc-mipi-csi2: don't require clock lane stop state for continuous clock sensors

dwc_csi_wait_for_phy_stopstate() unconditionally waits for the clock
lane to reach stop state along with the data lanes, causing stream
enable to fail:

  dwc-mipi-csi2 4ad30000.csi: Lanes are not in stop state(0xf)
  mxc-isi 4ad50000.isi: Failed to enable pipe 0

The check is waiting for something that legitimately doesn't happen
with this sensor, not a real link/wiring/timing fault: sensors using
a continuous clock (the default per the CSI-2 spec unless the
"clock-noncontinuous" endpoint property is present) keep the clock
lane in HS mode for as long as they are streaming and never return
it to stop state, while the data lanes idle normally between bursts.

Only require the clock lane stop state when the source endpoint is
configured for a non-continuous clock.

Signed-off-by: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate No time for upstreaming

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/nxp/dwc-mipi-csi2.c b/drivers/media/platform/nxp/dwc-mipi-csi2.c
index c6a375df2787..1a2b3c4d5e6f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/nxp/dwc-mipi-csi2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/nxp/dwc-mipi-csi2.c
@@ -708,9 +708,15 @@ static int dwc_csi_wait_for_phy_stopstate(struct dwc_csi_device *csidev)
 	u32 val;
 	int ret;
 
-	/* Check if lanes are in stop state */
-	phy_stopstate = CSI2RX_DPHY_STOPSTATE_CLK_LANE;
-	phy_stopstate |= GENMASK(csidev->bus.num_data_lanes - 1, 0);
+	/*
+	 * Check if lanes are in stop state. The clock lane only enters
+	 * stop state between frames for sensors using a non-continuous
+	 * clock; continuous-clock sensors keep it in HS mode.
+	 */
+	phy_stopstate = GENMASK(csidev->bus.num_data_lanes - 1, 0);
+	if (csidev->bus.flags & V4L2_MBUS_CSI2_NONCONTINUOUS_CLOCK)
+		phy_stopstate |= CSI2RX_DPHY_STOPSTATE_CLK_LANE;
+
 	ret = readl_poll_timeout(csidev->regs + CSI2RX_DPHY_STOPSTATE,
 				 val, (val & phy_stopstate) == phy_stopstate,
 				 10, 10000);
